opener landed at press (2026-11-28): a combo's window opener logged inside its own slow-down landed at the press.

What it does: replayrun.ts openerFirst, before makeCast: where a combo's window is shut at its frame, the pinned
landings due in its own stop (skillStops, from frame 0), in the log's order, are re-pinned at the press frame, as many
as open the window (the first that does and those logged before it). The combo-windows lead's 12 INSIDE lines but
8056 112.70 s went (and four combos no flag named: 9a80 1.57 s Si, b7b3 6.67, dbae 8.00, e989 63.57 s Arcane).

Measured (`measure --base 400bb44`): verified plain 78.5 → 78.2% (b7b3 49 → 48, dbae 67 → 66), development 84.3 →
84.1% (9a80 280 → 253 plain mixed, e989 267 → 264 worse, c4f3 468 → 470 better), hold-outs plain 82.6 → 80.9% (2
worse: plain −94, unquantified +91), every |damage error| unchanged.

Why dropped: a landing moved keeps nothing of what the log's frame gave it: the engine's frame-keyed logged facts
(loggedCrits, loggedModifiers, loggedReactionLevels: within a frame of the logged hit) miss a reaction it sets off
(4e5e 28.79 s: Estella's Cryst reaction lost its logged crit), and Arcane's own ultimate hits moved before her
combo's cast lost the combo's effects the log shows them with. The question is only the window's facts at the press,
so the kept rule (openerAhead) takes the window the opener opens and leaves the landings where the log has them. What
would make it work: a landing's moved frame that keeps its logged frame for those lookups, and a guard on the
combo's own cast-time effects (its value says which side of the cast it landed on).

